[Music]  if you're booting up Skyrim  special-edition expecting to be  overwhelmed by a transcendent visual  splendor you're much more likely to be  disappointed than blown away Skyrim's  visual upgrade is noticeable but by no  means incredible and many of its uglier  elements like it's off-putting character  models persist but here's the thing  that's totally ok the ps4 and Xbox one  versions visuals are now on par with the  game PC players have been enjoying for  years the brighter colors and crisper  textures make the experience more  immersive than ever for console owners  where previously for example enemies in  the dark might momentarily blend into  their blurry or muddy backgrounds  lighting and textures are now improved  to a point where visual sloppiness no  longer impacts gameplay patek and that's  the key Skyrim is without a question or  caveat one of the greatest RPGs ever  made the fact that console gamers can  now enjoy the experience even more is a  direct result of the remasters visual  updates a positive turn of events yes  it's somewhat disappointing that even  this updated version of Skyrim can't  match modern graphics but the game looks  objectively better as if a blurry gray  filter has suddenly been lifted and the  new visuals allow for an even deeper  appreciation of Skyrim's rich leveling  multifaceted combat vast open-world and  deep well of side content it was as big  as the mountain in blackest night  it's right over the barrel dragons now  is it please mother if you keep on like  this everyone in town will think you're  crazy that appreciation is further  deepened by another crucial improvement  shorter loading times previously ducking  into a shop or entering a dungeon would  trigger an impressively long loading  screen but now these same instances pass  in maybe a quarter of the time given how  frequently you encounter loading screens  in Skyrim that's actually a more  meaningful improvement than the upgraded  graphics Skyrim's infamous glitches seem  to have subsided as well at least to  some degree I did notice some characters  clipping through objects and my  companion randomly spawned at the bottom  of a cliff when I walked out of a  particular dungeon but I didn't  encounter any floating mammoths or  broken objectives in my companion when  he wasn't busy spawning in a weird place  did a decent job of staying out of the  way during comment  admittedly my time with the game thus  far has been brief I've played roughly  six hours on PlayStation 4 which is a  drop in the bucket compared to 150 hours  I spent on the original Skyrim on PC  there's still a chance however I'll  encounter more bugs as I progress  further into the game on the flip side I  also need to explore Skyrim's three  major DLC packs which are included in  the special edition as well as the  healthy collection of mods already  approved and available for console  players if you somehow miss Skyrim when  it originally launched five years ago  you owe it to yourself to play the game  and special edition is unquestionably  your new best option to do that and if  you did play Skyrim you now have a valid  excuse to return to Tamriel's snowy  northern region and complete all those  guild missions you missed the core game  feels just as engrossing and  exhilarating now as it did back in 2011  frankly the only players who don't stand  to gain anything from Special Edition  are PC players who've been consistently  modding and playing the game for the  past five years if that's not you Skyrim  special edition is an easy  recommendation  you

